 ('starting-facet-model','main',1,'Introduction; Figure 1 on p2','Cited starting-belt facet model','The cited starting wurtzite CdSe belts are five monolayers thick. Hypothetical unreconstructed top/bottom and long-edge facets are nonpolar, with four-coordinate valley atoms and three-coordinate ridge atoms before ligation. This is a cited structural model, not a new product refinement.','cited-starting-qb-model',[('cited core layers','5','monolayers'),('valley coordination','4','count'),('ridge coordination','3','count')],[]),
 ('starting-amine-model','main',1,'Introduction','Cited starting-belt amine stoichiometry','Prior elemental analysis gives CdSe[n-octylamine]0.53. The cited interpretation has an amine at each three-coordinate surface Cd or Se, as a datively bound Lewis base to Cd and pseudo-hydrogen-bond donor to Se; no new atomic structure is supplied.','cited-starting-qb-model',[('amine per CdSe','0.53','molecules per CdSe')],[]),
 ('prior-oleate-stoichiometry','main',1,'Introduction','Cited Z-type ligand model','The prior empirical formula CdSe[Cd(oleate)2]0.19 is interpreted as one Cd(oleate)2 per ridge Se; bridging adjacent Se atoms is proposed. This prior model is distinct from the current precursor and shell-growth experiments.','cited-ligation-model',[('Cd(oleate)2 per CdSe','0.19','molecules per CdSe')],[]),
